Z||000000||fierodave||10-09-2000||02:58 AM||||<BR>Hello all  Been under the weather  as of late, thanks for all the email with your prayers!<P>I can no longer offer the headliner & dash corner repairs I have been doing due to my illness so i'll pass along a few tips to you all!<P>I have had some x-lint results using Napa's Flex-bumper repair kits for my dash corner resto's,  it feathers into the dash perfectly,  and is as flexible  as the dash corners. <P>Cut out the damaged area, 36 grit the dash 1/2" around area to repair  and make a masking tape bridge to dam the mixed repair compond (it flows a little so the dam is needed)  <BR>Then finish the repair as the directions on the kit state.<P>The kit is Napa's Flex repair kit  part No.765-1540 <BR>It retails around $26.00  and one kit has done over 10 dash restos!<P>For the guys in the body shop trade  this kit is made for Napa BY Marson  <BR>It's a great product and you will have super results.  <BR>If you need more details  just give me a call, No emails Please  or post it here I'll try to keep an eye open for it  lol   <BR>FD<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/fierosig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 10-09-2000).]||||reg||1
